% \begin{enumerate}
% \item If only one vertex of $(p_i,p_j)$ is in $D'$, then choose the third edge of a line segment that is incident to that vertex in $D'$. If both vertices of $(p_i,p_j)$ are in $D'$ then choose the third edge of a line segment that is incident to either $p_i$ or $p_j$. 
% \item Next, choose every fourth edge from the chosen edge (excluding this edge) on each line segment by traversing through the line segments of $p_i \rightsquigarrow p_j$ until reaching $p_j$ (see Figure \ref{fig3} for illustration). 
