% % We can repeat the above process for other such paths in $G'$. However, if both or at least one of $p_i$ and $p_j$ is ev-dominated by edges outside $p_i\rightsquigarrow p_j$, then we can simply select all the incident edges at one of them and replace the edges in $E(p_i\rightsquigarrow p_j)\cap S^{ev}$ with their adjacent ones so that the other endpoint of $p_i\rightsquigarrow p_j$ is ev-dominated. Note that the cardinality of the updated $S^{ev}$ is still at most $3k'+l$, because $\sum_{i,j}(\lvert E(p_i\rightsquigarrow p_j)\cap S^{ev} \rvert -1)\leq l$, where $k'$ is a positive integer.
